(Bug #70 over a buffer destination: the clause is carried into a buffer
 append too. The analyzer judges such an append by the clause's subject -
 the parity #59 set, where a `treating`-wrapped read reports what a bare
 read of the same subject reports.)

a list called names is ["ann", "-"].

a buffer called built is 64 bytes.
append each name from names treating "-" as "anon" to built.
print built as text.

(The control: without the clause the same append is unchanged)
a buffer called plain is 64 bytes.
append each name from names to plain.
print plain as text.
